{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Indeed, etc.</b> The sense: like trees that vanished, as though they were never planted, from the nif'al binyan; זורעו from a binyan whose verbal noun is not used." "<b>without root.</b> Pa'al verb, the qal binyan." "<b>and also [He] blows.</b> Like נשפת ברוחך (Exodus 15:10), and the sense of וגם is 'moreover.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:13.099704736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}